Hiya.  Releasing the first version (esc01a) of my "Essences and Spell
Components" patch.  This version is contained in my overall patch
jdc03a, and is not available separately.  It is independent of my
other changes, though, so if you don't like my monk and ranger
changes, you can #undef them out (and ignore the extra entries in
data.base).

http://www.jcatena.net/nethack/patches.shtml#esc

Each spell cast now consumes a nonmagic material component.  Some
components are better than others, ranging from unsuitable (cast
likely to fail) to superb (cast more likely to succeed).  There is a
new item, the zester, which helps you get spell components.

I wrote an in-depth spoiler for this, since it changes a fundamental
part of the game, and to test it you need to know what to expect from
a given spell/component combination.

SPOILER: http://www.jcatena.net/nethack/esc-spoiler

If you have any additional suggestions for spell/component
combinations, please let me know. :)

